  "body": "Refs #900. Process change: PROCESS_VERSION 14 -> 15.\n\n## What changed\n- `xtask/src/exec.rs`: `cargo xtask gate` sets `RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache` and `SCCACHE_CACHE_SIZE=20G` for its cargo calls ONLY when `sccache` is on PATH; an existing `RUSTC_WRAPPER` or `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1` wins; without sccache nothing changes. Release packaging (`release.rs`) never uses it. Pinned by `the_compile_cache_is_enabled_only_when_sccache_exists_and_nobody_chose_otherwise`.\n- `Cargo.toml` (dev/test profiles only; release untouched): `[profile.dev] debug = \"line-tables-only\"`, deps `debug = false`, deps `opt-level` 2 -> 1.\n- Skills/agents (work-issue, resolve-conflicts, PR-reviewer): use the worktree's default `target/`, not a `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` env var (sccache hashes it -> 0 hits across worktrees).\n- AGENTS.md \"Testing\": short paragraph on the cache and how to enable it for plain cargo (`RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache`).\n- Not changed: no wrapper or linker in `.cargo/config.toml`.\n\nI installed sccache 0.8.2 on this machine (`cargo install sccache --locked`, user account; it was not installed before). Cache: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Mozilla\\sccache\\cache`, capped 20G.\n\n## Measurements (Windows MSVC, shared loaded machine, +-20%)\n`cargo test -p camcraft-app --test repair_model --no-run`, empty target:\n\n| Variant | cold build | target/ |\n|---|---|---|\n| baseline | 395 s | 2833 MB |\n| line-tables-only debug | 409 s | 1616 MB (-43%) |\n| + sccache, empty cache | 203-294 s | 1616 MB |\n| + sccache warm, other worktree path (opt 2) | 177 s | 1616 MB |\n| deps opt 1 / opt 0 (parallel, noisy) | 216 s / 114 s | 1536 / 1619 MB |\n\n- motion `--lib --no-run`: 73 s base; 40 s / 47 s with sccache cold/warm.\n- Cross-worktree hits: 161/207 cacheable Rust compiles (77.8%), only without a `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` env var (0 hits with it). Misses: our own path crates; 62 build scripts/proc-macros are non-cacheable.\n- C code (flecs via cc) is not cached: `CC=\"sccache cl\"` failed (cl not on PATH outside vcvars); not pursued.\n- dep opt-level vs run time, motion finish3d: opt2 46.7 s, opt1 48.7 s, opt0 142 s; flow 47/50 s -> opt 1 chosen. app import / pocket3d_hsm / adaptive_band are too short (<2 s) to discriminate.\n- Linker: rust-lld works but gains ~0.3 s per relink (2.1 vs 2.4 s) and flipping it rebuilds build scripts; left out (recommendation: not worth it).\n- Panics/backtraces keep file:line with line tables only (checked).\n\n## Not measured\nWarm-cache cold build with final settings (opt 1 + cache), quick/batch gate wall time, C-code caching, Linux/macOS. Done-means (3x faster, target <= half) not confirmed (target is 57%, ~2.2x faster), hence `Refs`, not `Fixes`. Folding the 266 app test binaries is out of scope.\n\n## Fork must do\nSync process files at PROCESS_VERSION 15 (xtask, skills, AGENTS.md); also takes `Cargo.toml` profile lines. Optional: `cargo install sccache --locked`.\n\n## Tests\nxtask unit tests: 32 passed. `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main --dry-run` plans batch (Cargo.toml changed); the full gate was not run to completion (stopped on request).\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium (no escalation)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
